<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">targeting</ansi>

Who each fighter aims at, and how a fight holds together.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Enemy groups</ansi>

Enemies that belong together (a band of bandits, a pack of wolves) fight as a
group, in a formation of two to five. Hostile creatures gather in groups:
the ones a place is known for spawn together, a rat and a ruffian if
that's what haunts the alley, never one alone. A lone survivor of a
broken group, or a straggler that wandered in, joins another idle group
there when it can; otherwise it lingers alone until the place brings it
company. Only a few great beasts always stand alone. Strike one member, and the whole group comes for you. A shopkeeper,
or someone you're talking with, isn't drawn into their group's fight.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">One battle at a time</ansi>

You and your company fight one group at a time: that's your battle. Any
other group that turns on you waits its turn, and doesn't strike while it
waits. When your battle ends, the group that turned on you first begins
the next one at once.

While another player is free in the same place, a waiting group turns on
them instead ("The ruffian and the others turn toward Brom."), and you each
fight your own battle.

You can't <ansi fg="command">attack</ansi> a waiting group until your battle is over; a bare
<ansi fg="command">attack</ansi> picks a foe from your battle. A harmful spell, a backstab, or a
shot at a waiting group is held too, and a waiting group's spells hold
off you. When you <ansi fg="command">flee</ansi>, only your battle's group can block the way.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Keeping everyone fighting</ansi>

At the start of each round, while your company and an enemy group are
fighting:

- any fighter, on either side, with no target, a fallen target, or a target
  they can't reach turns toward the weakest foe they can reach;
- a fighter whose target is still in reach keeps it;
- the enemy group's anger at you doesn't wear off while the fight lasts.

You're told when you turn (<ansi fg="command">You turn toward the bandit slinger.</ansi>), and see
when others do (<ansi fg="command">Garrick Vane turns toward the bandit bruiser.</ansi>).

A fighter who can reach no one waits, and strikes as soon as someone comes
into reach (when a front fighter falls, for example).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Stepping out</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">break</ansi> takes you out of the fight until you attack again, or the fight
ends. Your companions fight on, and enemies may keep attacking you.

<ansi fg="command">flee</ansi> tries to run out of the room. Your companions follow you. The fight
ends when nobody is fighting any more.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Alone</ansi>

With no companion beside you, you still fight one group at a time, and a
group whose target fell turns on you. But nothing turns you: you choose
each new target yourself.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help formation</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.
